rem Double pandigital number divisible
rem by 11
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=491

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

rem k_d copies of digit d sit in the
rem 10 odd places: sum k = 10, and 11
rem divides the number when sum d k_d
rem = 45 mod 11. Odd places hold 10! /
rem prod k! orders, 9! k_0 / prod k!
rem of them with a leading 0; even
rem places 10! / prod (2 - k)!. With k
rem in 0..2 the products are powers
rem of 2.
Ix = (0 till 3 ** 10) copy
Bs = array shape 10 fill 3
K = (Ix digits Bs) transpose
Ds = (0 till 10) copy
Ok = (K sum rank 1) equal 10
W = (K * Ds) sum rank 1
Ok = Ok and ((W - 45) mod 11 equal 0)
K = K (Ok indices)
C2 = (K equal 2) count rank 1
C0 = (K equal 0) count rank 1
K0 = K transpose 0
Od = (3628800 - 362880 * K0) // 2 ** C2
Ev = 3628800 // 2 ** C0
Answer = (Od * Ev) sum
Answer print
